sequenceDiagram
    actor C as Client
    participant AC as AuthenticationController
    participant US as UserService
    participant AM as AuthenticationManager
    participant UAP as UserAuthenticationProvider
    participant SAS as sessionAuthenticationStrategy
    participant SCR as SecurityContextRepository
    participant DB as Postgres (users, spring_session*)

    Note over C,DB: one of only two routes reachable without a session -- the other is /signin

    C->>AC: POST /api/signup {displayName (optional), email, password}

    alt request body fails Jakarta validation
        AC--xAC: MethodArgumentNotValidException (before this method body runs)
        AC-->>C: 400 ProblemDetail {code: VALIDATION_FAILED, errors: {field: message}}
    else request body valid
        AC->>US: userService.save(signupDTO)
        US->>DB: existsByEmail(email)
        alt email already registered
            DB-->>US: true
            US--xAC: throws AppDuplicateResourceException
            AC-->>C: 409 ProblemDetail {code: DUPLICATE_RESOURCE}
            Note over US,DB: a race between two simultaneous signups for the SAME address<br/>still cannot create two rows -- users.email carries a database-level<br/>unique constraint too (uk_users_email). The LOSER of that race hits<br/>DataIntegrityViolationException instead, backstopped by<br/>GlobalExceptionHandler's broader arm -- also 409, but with a<br/>different code: DATA_INTEGRITY_VIOLATION. A client may see either code.
        else email available
            DB-->>US: false
            US->>DB: INSERT INTO users
            DB-->>US: new UserEntity
            US-->>AC: createdUser
            Note over AC,SCR: everything from here to the response is IDENTICAL code to<br/>the signin flow -- see auth-signin-scenario.mmd for this same helper,<br/>drawn there in full including its own failure arms
            AC->>AC: build unauthenticated token from createdUser.id<br/>(the id, NOT the email address)
            AC->>AM: authenticationManager.authenticate(token)
            AM->>UAP: authenticate(token)
            UAP->>DB: loadUserByUsername(id)
            DB-->>UAP: stored credential
            UAP->>UAP: passwordEncoder.matches(password, storedHash)
            alt authenticate() reports success
                Note over UAP: builds a MINIMAL principal (username only, no password hash) --<br/>this is the object Spring Session serializes into the session store
                UAP-->>AM: Authentication(principal=User, no password)
                AM-->>AC: Authentication
                AC->>SAS: sessionAuthenticationStrategy.onAuthentication(authentication, request, response)
                Note over AC,SAS: the concurrent-session ceiling drawn on the signin diagram<br/>CANNOT reject a signup here -- a principal that did not exist a<br/>moment ago has zero live sessions. The session-id rotation half of<br/>this same strategy still applies.
                AC->>SCR: securityContextRepository.saveContext(context, request, response)
                Note over SCR,DB: written into a request-scoped session here -- the session<br/>rows are committed to Postgres only as the response is flushed,<br/>AFTER this handler has already returned. A client that inspects the<br/>database the instant it gets its response sees nothing yet.
                AC-->>C: 201 Set-Cookie: JSESSIONID (new session)<br/>Location: /api/users/me<br/>body {id, email, displayName, theme}
                Note right of C: the Location header names a resource with no GET handler<br/>yet (open todo since 2026-08-12) -- following it will not succeed
            else authenticate() reports failure (any exception collapses to false)
                AC->>US: userService.deleteById(createdUser.id)
                US->>DB: DELETE FROM users
                Note over AC: caught by this method's own blanket catch -- an<br/>AccessDeniedException is raised first, then re-thrown as<br/>BadCredentialsException, so the client sees 401, NOT 403,<br/>despite the intermediate exception type
                AC-->>C: 401 ProblemDetail {code: BAD_CREDENTIALS}
            end
        end
    end
